@{h1}Syntax (incomplete)

Program directives and top-level items, where declarations and statements may
appear.

<program>         ::= [ <make> ]
                      [ <org> ]
                      { <top_level_item> }

<top_level_item>  ::= <decl>
                    | <statement>

<make>            ::= "make" [ "dot" | "nex" | "raw" ] "(" <string> ")" ";"

<org>             ::= "org" <number> ";"

<bank>            ::= "bank" "(" <bankno> [ "," <bankno> ] ")" <stmnt_block>

The bank directive is used to target code for specific banks. This is 
useful when compiling NEX or direct to memory binaries. Banks contain 
blocks of code and data.

<bankno> - The bank that the block of code will be compiled and assembled for. <statements> - The code that will be included in this bank

Example: Compile code for bank 40

bank 40 {
  for(char ch='A'; ch<='Z'; ch=ch+1) {
    putc(ch)
  }
}
